# Gate-owned paths — Nishfleet/0509
#
# Everything listed here is machinery that DECIDES whether other changes may
# land: the workflows that produce the required status contexts, the decision
# scripts those workflows run, the scanner ignore files, and the design-system
# ratchet with its ceilings. A pull request that edits one of these is not
# shipping a feature; it is changing the rules the fleet is judged by, and that
# is Nish's call.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING THE FILE
# ----------------------------------
# On GitHub, CODEOWNERS by itself blocks NOTHING. It only auto-requests review.
# The blocking behaviour comes from branch protection's
# `require_code_owner_reviews`, and that setting is deliberately NOT enabled on
# `main` for a reason that is structural rather than a matter of taste:
#
#   Nishfleet/0509 has exactly ONE collaborator. `gh api orgs/Nishfleet` reports
#   `filled_seats: 1`, and every pull request in the recent history is authored
#   AND merged by nish3451, because the fleet's workers hold that identity's
#   token. GitHub forbids approving your own pull request. Turning on
#   `require_code_owner_reviews` with @nish3451 as the owner would therefore not
#   gate gate-path PRs — it would make them permanently unmergeable, including
#   the ones Nish writes himself. That is not a stricter gate, it is a deadlock,
#   and the predictable response to a deadlock is an `--admin` bypass, which
#   destroys the audit trail the gate exists to create. (Same finding, same
#   remedy as the sole-admin attestation path in
#   .github/workflows/required-verifier-integrity.yml, Nish, 2026-08-20.)
#
# What actually enforces these paths today, mechanically, regardless of who is
# pressing the button:
#
#   * `enforce_admins: true` on `main` — required checks bind admins too, so
#     `gh pr merge --admin` can no longer skip a red check.
#   * `required-verifier-integrity` — a required context that fails any PR
#     touching the listed verifier definitions without an independent admin
#     approval or a current sole-admin attestation.
#   * `gate-integrity` — a required context that fails any PR which deletes or
#     skips tests, raises a design-ratchet ceiling, widens a scanner ignore
#     file, softens a CI step, or edits any path in this file, unless it carries
#     the matching justification.
#
# So this file is the DOCUMENTED OWNERSHIP MAP and the source of the gate-path
# list; the two required checks are the teeth. Turn on
# `require_code_owner_reviews` the moment a second admin exists on this
# repository — at that point it becomes the best control of the three, and the
# attestation paths should be retired in the same change.

# Everything, by default, so a new gate file is never accidentally unowned.
*                                       @nish3451

# CI definitions: the workflows that produce every required status context.
/.github/workflows/                     @nish3451
/.github/CODEOWNERS                     @nish3451

# The gates' own decision logic and its deterministic fixture regressions.
/.github/scripts/                       @nish3451

# Scanner configuration. Widening an ignore file is the quietest way to land a
# finding the gate was built to catch.
/.gitleaksignore                        @nish3451
/.gitleaks.toml                         @nish3451
/.semgrepignore                         @nish3451
/.semgrep.yml                           @nish3451
/.semgrep.yaml                          @nish3451

# The design-system ratchet: the script that counts retired markers and the
# frozen ceilings it counts against. Raising a ceiling is invisible to the
# ratchet's own test, which reads whatever number the same PR just wrote.
/scripts/design-system-ratchet.mjs      @nish3451
/docs/design-system-ratchet.json        @nish3451

# CI runner and release-verification scripts invoked by the required contexts.
/scripts/ci-vitest-run.sh               @nish3451
/scripts/ci-verify-production-candidate.sh  @nish3451
/scripts/ci-verify-provider-main-cas.sh @nish3451

# The production deploy-authorization chain.
/.github/workflows/deploy-production.yml      @nish3451
/.github/workflows/finalize-production-soak.yml @nish3451
